Venetium 0029 - on Windows ARM32, sandboxed child processes are created without PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_MITIGATION_POLICY.

BATCH-ARM-FIX-2, his decision (2026-10-04, Q1 "both in one trip": ship this now, and carry probe v3, which measures the older
4-byte form of the attribute and the in-child mitigation calls, for a possible later restoration).

On the Surface 2 (Windows 10 build 15035 ARM32, the post-0028 zip) sandboxed child launches fail:
- trip 3's metrics recorded Process.Sandbox.Launch.Error = 87 (ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER) x14, and SBOX_ERROR_CREATE_PROCESS for the
  GPU, renderers and the storage service;
- the DEVICE-3 runs log "GPU process launch failed: error_code=18" (SBOX_ERROR_CREATE_PROCESS) until the browser's intentional
  "GPU process isn't usable" crash.

The sandbox probe (sbxprobe 2, run on the device) measured the cause:
- build 15035 ARM32 refuses PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_MITIGATION_POLICY for every value, 0 included, in both the 8-byte and the
  16-byte form, through CreateProcessW and CreateProcessAsUserW alike;
- every other part of Chromium's call is accepted: flags 0x0008040C, STARTF 0x180, JOB_LIST, CHILD_PROCESS_POLICY, HANDLE_LIST
  with Chromium-like handles, every token level, the alternate window station and the filtered environment (COMPONENT_FILTER
  fails at Update with NOT_SUPPORTED, which Chromium already tolerates);
- with only that attribute removed, all 11 replays of Chromium's call were accepted, including the one with the real
  venetium.exe.

1 file:
- sandbox/win/src/startup_information_helper.cc: under #if defined(_M_ARM), SetMitigations() clears the mitigation word (both
  DWORD64s) and its size after ConvertProcessMitigationsToPolicy(). CountAttributes() and BuildStartupInformation() therefore leave
  the attribute out. Every other architecture is unchanged.

What this changes on ARM32, per creation-time mitigation Chromium requests on this OS (GPU / renderer / storage service; the
renderer with code integrity adds one):
- Never applied now (nothing re-applies them):
  - EXTENSION_POINT_DISABLE, FONT_DISABLE (non-system fonts), IMAGE_LOAD_NO_REMOTE, IMAGE_LOAD_NO_LOW_LABEL - all types;
  - WIN32K_SYSTEM_CALL_DISABLE - renderer and storage service. Their sandbox config still requests win32k lockdown, including its
    fake-GDI interceptions, while win32k now stays usable in those processes (see ARM-FIX-2-RESULTS.md).
- Still applied another way:
  - HEAP_TERMINATE: base::EnableTerminationOnHeapCorruption() at process start in every content process;
  - BOTTOM_UP_ASLR: the broker's weak 32-bit emulation (ApplyProcessMitigationsToSuspendedProcess);
  - BLOCK_NON_MICROSOFT_BINARIES for the code-integrity renderer: after startup, through the delayed set; only the startup window
    is lost.
- Unchanged: tokens, integrity levels, jobs, desktops, the handle list, the child-process policy, and the delayed mitigations each
  child applies to itself (DLL search order, Microsoft-signed binaries only, strict handle checks, dynamic-code disable where
  Chromium asks for it). Those in-child calls are PCHECKed and have not run on 15035 ARM32; probe v3 measures them.

Checked (STRUCTURAL):
- The ARM startup_information_helper.obj's SetMitigations zeroes the 16-byte word and the size right after the conversion.
- The preprocessed source is identical with and without this patch for i686, x86_64, aarch64 and arm64ec (review).
- Relinked chrome.dll and venetium.exe are ARMNT with ASLR/DEP/CFG, with the same sections, exports, version strings and import
  sets, 0 imports missing in the device's 15035 kernel32/ntdll, and the __rt_* division shim present. chrome_elf.dll is unchanged.

NOT MEASURED: whether this clears the launch failure on the device (his re-run).

diff --git a/sandbox/win/src/startup_information_helper.cc b/sandbox/win/src/startup_information_helper.cc
index fce8b01..e885141 100644
--- a/sandbox/win/src/startup_information_helper.cc
+++ b/sandbox/win/src/startup_information_helper.cc
@@ -43,6 +43,18 @@ void StartupInformationHelper::SetDesktop(std::wstring desktop) {
 void StartupInformationHelper::SetMitigations(MitigationFlags flags) {
   ConvertProcessMitigationsToPolicy(flags, &mitigations_[0],
                                     &mitigations_size_);
+#if defined(_M_ARM)
+  // Venetium 0029: Windows 10 build 15035 on ARM32 refuses CreateProcess with
+  // ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER whenever PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_MITIGATION_POLICY is
+  // in the attribute list - for every value, 0 included, in both the 8- and the
+  // 16-byte form (measured on the device). So on ARM32 sandboxed children are
+  // created without it: the creation-time mitigations are not applied at
+  // launch there. The mitigations a child applies to itself after startup
+  // (delayed mitigations) are unchanged.
+  mitigations_[0] = 0;
+  mitigations_[1] = 0;
+  mitigations_size_ = 0;
+#endif
   ConvertProcessMitigationsToComponentFilter(flags, &component_filter_);
 }
 
